31,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"We are spending about 2,300 yen monthly on supplies, often duplicating items. Professional cleaning is 4,200 yen per hour.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,A full pass takes about 102 minutes. An outside firm requires us to tidy up before they even arrive.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Usage is uneven; a few of us do all the cooking. Also, some of us are away for weeks at a time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The bathroom grout spoils in eleven days regardless of effort. Plus, we all have different definitions of ""clean.""","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,Previous tenants tried permanent assignments and stopped speaking. Most of our fights start with reminders about undone chores.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, if usage is uneven, a flat split of costs or labor might feel unfair to some.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we hire a firm, we still have to tidy up, so it doesn't fully remove the burden.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Exactly. A fixed rota ignores the fact that some people are barely here to make a mess.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"If the bathroom is a lost cause due to ventilation, maybe we should just accept a professional standard.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,We must avoid permanent assignments. It sounds like a recipe for resentment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"A paid service would be the most consistent, but we need to be clear on how the billing is handled.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Two hours of work a week isn't huge, but the mental load of the rota is what's draining.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I'm leaning toward something that accounts for actual presence and usage.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"I just want a standard. If we can't agree on what ""done"" means, we need a third party.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"A rota might lead to those ""reminders"" that cause rows. A service removes the conflict.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,Let's consider the options. A service is expensive but removes the interpersonal friction.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Standing assignments are out, based on Midori's findings.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A rota is the traditional way, but it's often the most contested.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I'm tired of the bathroom. I vote for the most reliable option.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree with May. Let's prioritize our relationship over the cost.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
